###
### Subify OS API — HTTP smoke tests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client)
###
### Preferred interactive UI (Development):
###   Scalar:     {{host}}/scalar/v1
###   OpenAPI:    {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
###   Root:       {{host}}/  → redirects to Scalar
###
### Run API:
###   cd api/Subify.Api && dotnet run --launch-profile http
###

@host = http://localhost:5240
@contentType = application/json

# After a successful login, paste tokens here for future authenticated requests:
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Docs — open Scalar UI in browser
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name scalarUi
GET {{host}}/scalar/v1
Accept: text/html

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Docs — OpenAPI document (JSON)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name openApiDocument
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Health — liveness (container probe)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name healthLive
GET {{host}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Health — readiness (Postgres reachable)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name healthReady
GET {{host}}/health/ready
Accept: application/json

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Register
### Body: RegisterCommand { fullName, email, password }
### 201 Created → RegisterResponse { email, message, userId, expiration }
### 409 Conflict → email already registered
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Onur Karakuş",
  "email": "onur@test.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Register (duplicate email — expect 409)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name registerDuplicate
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Duplicate User",
  "email": "onur@test.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Login
### Body: LoginCommand { email, password }
### 200 OK → LoginResponse { email, accessToken, refreshToken, expiration }
###
### Note: Login currently requires EmailConfirmed=true on the user.
### If register left EmailConfirmed=false, confirm in DB or adjust policy (task 3.2.9).
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "onur@test.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Login (invalid credentials — expect 401 / problem details)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name loginInvalid
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "onur@test.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword1!"
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Auth — Login validation failure (empty body fields — expect 400 VAL)
### Pipeline: ValidationBehavior + LoginValidator → ProblemDetails.errors
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name loginValidationFail
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "",
  "password": ""
}

###

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Example: authenticated call (Bearer)
### Uncomment / add endpoints as they land (profile, subscriptions, …).
### accessToken is filled from # @name login when using REST Client chain.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name mePlaceholder
# GET {{host}}/api/profile
# Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
# Accept: application/json
